{"seq":8,"slug":"knowledge-management-pkm","title":"知识管理与 PKM","stage":"DONE","category":"learning","chapterCount":5,"docCount":20,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm","rating":{"composite":4.01,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4.6,"coverage":4,"positioning":4,"strategic":3.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.87,"verdict":"consider","uScore":4}},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"知识管理与-pkm-简介\">知识管理与 PKM 简介</h1><p>个人知识管理（Personal Knowledge Management，简称 PKM）是一套关于如何系统性地捕获、组织、连接和运用知识的方法论。在信息过载的时代，我们每天接触海量的文章、书籍、播客和对话，但真正能转化为长期能力的知识少之又少。PKM 的核心目标不是囤积信息，而是构建一个能够持续产出洞见的思维系统——一个值得信赖的&quot;第二大脑&quot;。</p>\n<p>从 Niklas Luhmann 的卡片盒到 Tiago Forte 的 PARA 方法，从 Obsidian 的双向链接到间隔重复的记忆曲线，知识管理领域在过去十年经历了一场深刻的变革。数字工具让曾经只属于少数学者的知识管理方法变得触手可及，而网状结构的笔记系统正在取代传统的线性文件夹，成为知识组织的新范式。</p>\n<p>本知识库面向所有希望建立个人知识体系的学习者和创作者。无论你是刚接触笔记方法的新手，还是已经积累了数千条笔记却苦于无法有效检索和复用的老手，这里都将为你提供从理论到实践的完整指引。</p>\n<p>全书共分五个章节：</p>\n<p>第一章<strong>PKM 基础</strong>从什么是个人知识管理出发，辨析信息与知识的本质区别，建立捕获、组织、检索的基本框架，并介绍&quot;构建第二大脑&quot;的核心理念。</p>\n<p>第二章<strong>笔记方法论</strong>系统讲解四种经过验证的笔记方法——Zettelkasten 卡片笔记法、常青笔记、渐进式总结和原子笔记，帮助你找到最适合自己思维方式的记录策略。</p>\n<p>第三章<strong>工具与工作流</strong>深入 Obsidian、Logseq、Notion 三款主流知识管理工具，分析各自的设计哲学与适用场景，并探讨工具间的互操作性与数据迁移方案。</p>\n<p>第四章<strong>知识图谱</strong>探索链接与反向链接的机制，培养图式思维，讨论标签与文件夹之争，以及如何通过网状结构促成知识的涌现与意外发现。</p>\n<p>第五章<strong>学习系统</strong>围绕间隔重复、刻意练习、费曼技巧和阅读工作流展开，将知识管理延伸为一套完整的终身学习体系。</p>\n<p>建议按章节顺序阅读。前两章建立理论基础与方法论认知，第三章落地为具体的工具实践，第四章提升知识连接与结构化思维的能力，第五章将所有知识管理技能融合为可持续的学习系统。如果你已有 PKM 基础，可直接跳到第三章或第四章。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"pkm-fundamentals","title":"PKM 基础","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/pkm-fundamentals","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"what-is-pkm","title":"什么是个人知识管理 (PKM)","url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/pkm-fundamentals/what-is-pkm"},{"seq":2,"slug":"information-vs-knowledge","title":"信息与知识的区别","url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/pkm-fundamentals/information-vs-knowledge"},{"seq":3,"slug":"capture-organize-retrieve","title":"捕获、组织与检索","url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/pkm-fundamentals/capture-organize-retrieve"},{"seq":4,"slug":"building-a-second-brain","title":"构建第二大脑 (Building a Second Brain)","url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/pkm-fundamentals/building-a-second-brain"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"note-taking-methods","title":"笔记方法论","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/note-taking-methods","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"zettelkasten-method","title":"卡片盒笔记法 (Zettelkasten)","url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/note-taking-methods/zettelkasten-method"},{"seq":2,"slug":"evergreen-notes","title":"常青笔记 (Evergreen Notes)","url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/note-taking-methods/evergreen-notes"},{"seq":3,"slug":"progressive-summarization","title":"渐进式总结 (Progressive Summarization)","url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/note-taking-methods/progressive-summarization"},{"seq":4,"slug":"atomic-notes","title":"原子化笔记 (Atomic Notes)","url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/note-taking-methods/atomic-notes"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"tools-and-workflows","title":"工具与工作流","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/tools-and-workflows","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"obsidian-deep-dive","title":"Obsidian 深度解析","url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/tools-and-workflows/obsidian-deep-dive"},{"seq":2,"slug":"logseq-and-outlining","title":"Logseq 与大纲笔记法","url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/tools-and-workflows/logseq-and-outlining"},{"seq":3,"slug":"notion-for-teams","title":"Notion 团队协作","url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/tools-and-workflows/notion-for-teams"},{"seq":4,"slug":"tool-interoperability","title":"笔记工具互操作性","url":"/l-doc-books/h/learning/knowledge-management-pkm/tools-and-workflows/tool-interoperability"}]}